        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "During a trip，a car traveled a total of 570 miles on city roads and highways and used a total of\n19 gallons of gas．The car traveled an average of 26 miles per gallon of gas on city roads and 31\nmiles per gallon of gas on highways．Which system of equations represents this situation，\nwhere $c$ is the number of miles the car traveled on city roads and $h$ is the number of miles the car\ntraveled on highways？"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-bb52ff2b1da140e484fb53374fc8ceb5",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q15"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$c+h=19 c/26+h/31$ =\n$$570$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$c+h=19 26 c+31 h$$\n= 570"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$c+h=570 c/26+h/31$ =\n$$19$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$c+h=570 26 c+31$$\n$$h=19$$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
